[{:db/id 17592186105860 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2365a6d7-b820-5041-9972-25df8cfa8866"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2365a6d7-b820-5041-9972-25df8cfa8866" :question/id #uuid "2365a6d7-b820-5041-9972-25df8cfa8866" :question/math-academy-id "q-86922" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n\nI. The outcome of rolling a $10$-sided die\n\nII. The number of aces in a standard deck of playing cards\n\nIII. The weight of a randomly selected person, measured in kilograms" :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/05/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $1,2,3,…,10,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement II does *not* describe a continuous random variable. The number of aces in a standard deck of playing cards is not the outcome of a trial or experiment. (By definition, there are $4$ aces in a standard deck of playing cards.)\n\n- Statement III describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real numbers in the interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-375ee444-4376-5150-bb9c-79b09c44be67"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-375ee444-4376-5150-bb9c-79b09c44be67" :answer-field/id #uuid "375ee444-4376-5150-bb9c-79b09c44be67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5796bd74-a234-55f5-a5f9-bee4c20f2c37" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec8ef8d9-7011-5f21-8ec2-2534d66acfdf" "answer-c53010b8-a034-5aca-8828-82b8098d48fa" "answer-4eedb5eb-4a53-52bf-bb91-736a768c01a5" "answer-6e08cddb-71c7-54e2-99d5-5e60caa26d2f" "answer-5796bd74-a234-55f5-a5f9-bee4c20f2c37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec8ef8d9-7011-5f21-8ec2-2534d66acfdf" :answer/id #uuid "ec8ef8d9-7011-5f21-8ec2-2534d66acfdf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c53010b8-a034-5aca-8828-82b8098d48fa" :answer/id #uuid "c53010b8-a034-5aca-8828-82b8098d48fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4eedb5eb-4a53-52bf-bb91-736a768c01a5" :answer/id #uuid "4eedb5eb-4a53-52bf-bb91-736a768c01a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e08cddb-71c7-54e2-99d5-5e60caa26d2f" :answer/id #uuid "6e08cddb-71c7-54e2-99d5-5e60caa26d2f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5796bd74-a234-55f5-a5f9-bee4c20f2c37" :answer/id #uuid "5796bd74-a234-55f5-a5f9-bee4c20f2c37" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119744 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2ea583ed-35c3-538b-b597-43518611b1ac"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2ea583ed-35c3-538b-b597-43518611b1ac" :question/id #uuid "2ea583ed-35c3-538b-b597-43518611b1ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-77072" :question/problem "![](images/01/014c2310bcac5b6e9c2be2107bf8a5613b689ff29a8018d2be74fc607dd996db.png)\n\nFind the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨7-2{t}^{3},3{t}^{2}+10⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7-2{t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}+10)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6{t}^{2},\\,6t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-6{t}^{2})^{2}+(6t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{t}^{4}+36{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{t}^{2}({t}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =6t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,\\sqrt{3}].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}6t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u={t}^{2}+1$, $\\text{d}u=2t\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}3\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot 2t\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}3\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =2{u}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =2(8-1) \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8c3bd452-520c-5cac-8263-6875362cc4e5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8c3bd452-520c-5cac-8263-6875362cc4e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "8c3bd452-520c-5cac-8263-6875362cc4e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-da2916dc-97c4-51c9-852e-307c5a102816" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56a2e6b5-5884-5570-aa94-176a32aa11de" "answer-da2916dc-97c4-51c9-852e-307c5a102816" "answer-4ed9d04a-f96a-5183-9fc4-8dcfd77061e7" "answer-6e1ffe30-2504-50cd-8a45-20ca6353d983" "answer-9778e0bb-2590-5c24-908d-c9bf4daf3a54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56a2e6b5-5884-5570-aa94-176a32aa11de" :answer/id #uuid "56a2e6b5-5884-5570-aa94-176a32aa11de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da2916dc-97c4-51c9-852e-307c5a102816" :answer/id #uuid "da2916dc-97c4-51c9-852e-307c5a102816" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ed9d04a-f96a-5183-9fc4-8dcfd77061e7" :answer/id #uuid "4ed9d04a-f96a-5183-9fc4-8dcfd77061e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e1ffe30-2504-50cd-8a45-20ca6353d983" :answer/id #uuid "6e1ffe30-2504-50cd-8a45-20ca6353d983" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9778e0bb-2590-5c24-908d-c9bf4daf3a54" :answer/id #uuid "9778e0bb-2590-5c24-908d-c9bf4daf3a54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186304694 :answer-field/correct "answer-06570ee4-ef32-50c5-80dd-d62ee7471554" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06570ee4-ef32-50c5-80dd-d62ee7471554"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06570ee4-ef32-50c5-80dd-d62ee7471554" :answer/id #uuid "06570ee4-ef32-50c5-80dd-d62ee7471554" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8xe^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186119843 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-eec69fbf-a0cd-50e6-9b17-0f0c96351008"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-eec69fbf-a0cd-50e6-9b17-0f0c96351008" :question/id #uuid "eec69fbf-a0cd-50e6-9b17-0f0c96351008" :question/math-academy-id "q-69953" :question/problem "$|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|=$" :question/worked-solution "The $1$st row of the matrix contains three zeros, more than any other row. So using a Laplace expansion along the $1$st row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+1\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+3}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ed337fba-8f9c-5284-b664-f31a93279b80"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ed337fba-8f9c-5284-b664-f31a93279b80" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed337fba-8f9c-5284-b664-f31a93279b80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-d00a3088-dd85-511b-a78d-c803fdd41730" :answer-field/choices ["answer-394cf326-2a8e-53d3-b6bb-9d00bbd00896" "answer-cdaba3a2-4f44-5d67-97c9-41759abf06af" "answer-fb0c8f0c-3314-5bf3-83d0-87976ede682e" "answer-e302e086-65fb-5d1c-95c1-38d5bea87093" "answer-d00a3088-dd85-511b-a78d-c803fdd41730"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-394cf326-2a8e-53d3-b6bb-9d00bbd00896" :answer/id #uuid "394cf326-2a8e-53d3-b6bb-9d00bbd00896" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cdaba3a2-4f44-5d67-97c9-41759abf06af" :answer/id #uuid "cdaba3a2-4f44-5d67-97c9-41759abf06af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb0c8f0c-3314-5bf3-83d0-87976ede682e" :answer/id #uuid "fb0c8f0c-3314-5bf3-83d0-87976ede682e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e302e086-65fb-5d1c-95c1-38d5bea87093" :answer/id #uuid "e302e086-65fb-5d1c-95c1-38d5bea87093" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d00a3088-dd85-511b-a78d-c803fdd41730" :answer/id #uuid "d00a3088-dd85-511b-a78d-c803fdd41730" :answer/type :answer.t